# over the right shoulder, looking where the bot looks (pitched 20 degrees down). Each line overwrites the one before
# when its spots are open air, so the last that fits wins, most preferred last: the bot's own eyes (never inside a
# block), above its head looking down (a shaft it digs), then 1.5, 2.3 and 3.2 blocks behind. A wall pulls the camera
# in instead of hiding the bot.
execute as @a[tag=muse_cam_target,limit=1] at @s anchored eyes positioned ^ ^ ^ rotated ~ 20 run tp @e[type=minecraft:item_display,tag=muse_cam_eye,limit=1] ~ ~ ~ ~ ~
